From: oplus-sukisu_kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] fs/proc/task_mmu: re-apply both SUS_MAP checks for 6.12.30+

Derived from the two SUS_MAP hunks in susfs4ksu's
kernel_patches/50_add_susfs_in_gki-android16-6.12.patch.

GKI android16-6.12 (6.12.30+) refactored show_smaps_rollup(), so those two
hunks reject on our base. This re-applies them against the refactored
function. Both checks are required:

  1. at the top of the do-loop, for the normal path
  2. after vma_next() inside the mmap_lock_is_contended block, because the
     lock was dropped and re-acquired, so the vma may have been replaced

Dropping either one leaves SUS_MAP mappings visible in
/proc/<pid>/smaps_rollup.

The build applies this only when fs/proc/task_mmu.c.rej exists.

diff --git a/fs/proc/task_mmu.c b/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
index fc65fc3..20d2b50 100644
--- a/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
+++ b/fs/proc/task_mmu.c
@@ -1438,6 +1438,12 @@ static int show_smaps_rollup(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 
 	vma_start = vma->vm_start;
 	do {
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP
+		if (vma->vm_file && SUSFS_IS_INODE_SUS_MAP(file_inode(vma->vm_file))) {
+			last_vma_end = vma->vm_end;
+			continue;
+		}
+#endif // #ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP
 		smap_gather_stats(vma, &mss, 0);
 		last_vma_end = vma->vm_end;
 
@@ -1502,6 +1508,13 @@ static int show_smaps_rollup(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 			if (!vma)
 				break;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP
+			if (vma->vm_file && SUSFS_IS_INODE_SUS_MAP(file_inode(vma->vm_file))) {
+				last_vma_end = vma->vm_end;
+				continue;
+			}
+#endif // #ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP
+
 			/* Case 1 and 2 above */
 			if (vma->vm_start >= last_vma_end) {
 				smap_gather_stats(vma, &mss, 0);
